The answer is: ...came to a cabin in the woods. They heard a noise, and one man said, "That's the wind." The other man said, "No, that's the bear." They argued, and one man said, "I bet you ten dollars it's the wind." The other man took him up on the bet, and they both listened carefully. After a while, the man who bet on the wind said, "You know what? I was wrong. It's the bear." The other man said, "Yes, it's the bear." So, the man who bet on the wind lost ten dollars. What happened next?

The correct answer is: The man who bet on the bear said, "I'll tell you what. You give me that ten dollars, and I'll show you the bear." The other man said, "No, no, no. First you have to prove it." The man who bet on the bear said, "All right, all right. I'll show you the bear anyway." He went outside and called the bear with a bear call. The bear came up to him, and he pushed the bear back with his hands on its chest. The bear didn't charge him. The other man said, "You see? That's because you're an old hand at this." The man who bet on the bear said, "No, no, no. You see, I wasn't born here. I came here from the south. In the south, we don't have bears. That's why I had to prove it to you."


