The answer is: ...came to a cabin in the woods. The night was quiet and dark, save for the flickering of the fire in the hearth and the howling of wolves in the distance. The men talked of many things, but soon their conversation turned to the stories they had heard of the ghostly white creature that roamed the woods at night. They spoke of its cold, icy touch and its piercing, eerie scream. They spoke of the terrible fate that befall those who were unfortunate enough to encounter it in the forest. As the men spoke, the fire in the hearth began to burn low and the cabin grew cold. The night grew late and the howling of the wolves grew louder, closer. The two men shivered in the cabin, afraid to go outside. Suddenly, there was a knock at the door. The men jumped up, drawn to the door as if by some invisible force. They opened the door and there, in the moonlight, stood the white creature. It touched them with its icy hands and then, without a sound, vanished into the night. The men were left standing in the empty cabin, trembling with fear. They knew that they had encountered the Ghost of Egulac.


